The idea is to intercept evaluation when the object is involved, then search the stack for the assignment and rewrite it so your upvalue applies. The suggested pattern is:

`_Obj := Block[{Obj},
  Obj /: (Obj[id_]["Property"] = value_) := setObjProperty[id, value];
  With[{set = Cases[Stack[_], HoldForm[L_ = R_]?(FreeQ[#, Obj] &) :> ((# = R) &@L), 1, 1]},
    Return[set[[1]], Set] /; set =!= {}
  ]
]`

With this, `obj = Obj[1]; obj["Property"] = 256;` updates `properties` to `{256}`.

It’s acknowledged to add significant overhead and may be unacceptable for production use.

