Since the matrix is 10×9 and has full column rank 9, you can reduce it to a square 9×9 system by taking the first 9 rows, as in the accepted answer. Then compute the determinant of that square matrix and use Cramer’s rule:

solvefor[i_] := Module[{B},
  B = M;
  B[[All, i]] = b;
  Det[B]/Det[M]
]

This gives x_i without solving for all components at once. The provided solution specifically shows this works for example x1.

