Use the 4th-order Runge-Kutta update as a one-step map for your system, then repeat it over the interval.

A functional form is:

RungeKutta[func_List, yinit_List, y_List, step_] :=
 Module[{k1, k2, k3, k4},
  k1 = step N[func /. MapThread[Rule, {y, yinit}]];
  k2 = step N[func /. MapThread[Rule, {y, k1/2 + yinit}]];
  k3 = step N[func /. MapThread[Rule, {y, k2/2 + yinit}]];
  k4 = step N[func /. MapThread[Rule, {y, k3 + yinit}]];
  yinit + Total[{k1, 2 k2, 2 k3, k4}]/6
 ]

Here, func is the list of right-hand sides of your ODEs, yinit is the list of initial values, y is the list of variables, and step is the step size.

To solve the IVP, iterate it with:

NestList[RungeKutta[func, #, y, step] &, N[yinit], Round[t/step]]

where t is the final time.

If needed, add checks that the lists have the same length.

