You can’t “exit” the innermost pure function in a special imperative way from the code shown. The issue is that /; (Condition) has HoldAll, so in your version it holds the whole If[...] expression unevaluated while it tests !fail. That means fail never gets set before the condition is checked.

What works is to evaluate the code first, store its result, then apply /; to that result:

F[x_] := Block[{ans, success},
  ans = If[x >= 0, success = 1; Sqrt[x], success = 0];
  ans /; (success == 1)
]

Equivalent form:

F[x_] := Block[{ans, success},
  ans = If[x >= 0, success = 1; Sqrt[x], success = 0];
  Condition[ans, success == 1]
]

This supports leaving the expression unevaluated only when the condition fails.

