The working approach is to avoid sorting by absolute value during plotting, because that can cause pairwise swaps and vertical garbage at degeneracies. Instead, use a reference point (the origin) to evaluate the eigenvalues once, determine which bands you want there, and then plot those bands using a simple Sort[] with the chosen indices.

So the supported guidance is:
- plain Sort[] by function values can separate the sheets and avoid jumping;
- Sort[..., Abs[#1] <= Abs[#2] &] can still fail near symmetric crossings;
- a reference-point-based selection of bands is the more robust solution for controlling which eigenvalue sheets to plot.

