To plot the result in Mathematica, first make the sine wave time-limited with UnitStep, then convolve it with the Dirac delta.

One direct way is:

```mathematica
Clear[t, z];
f1 = DiracDelta[t - 10];
f2 = UnitStep[t] UnitStep[Pi - t] Sin[t];
conv = Convolve[f1, f2, t, z];
Plot[conv, {z, 0, 50}, Exclusions -> None]
```

This gives a shifted copy of the sine segment:
`-Sin[10 - z]` for `10 <= z <= 10 + Pi`, and 0 elsewhere.

