list = {{1, 2, 3}, {4, 5}, {6}};
list ~Flatten~ {2} ~Total~ {2}

This returns {11, 7, 3}.

So instead of looping and conditionally checking lengths, the concise way is to reshape the ragged list with Flatten[..., {2}] and then sum each resulting sublist with Total[..., {2}].

