Mathematica can’t directly detect “how many outputs are requested” from a normal function call. The supported workaround here is to use `Set` upvalues plus a helper variable like `nargout` to infer the left-hand side assignment context.

A proof-of-concept is:

```mathematica
ClearAll[f, ff]
f /: Set[arg_Symbol, f[x_]] := Block[{nargout = 1}, arg = ff[x]];
f /: Set[args_List, f[x_]] := Block[{nargout = Length[args]}, args = ff[x]];
f[arg_] /; FreeQ[Stack[], Set] := Block[{nargout = 1}, ff[arg]];
ff[x_] := Table[x, {nargout}]
```

