The discrepancy is due to Mathematica 7 mishandling that nested integration order, not because the expressions are mathematically different. With the order

{ux,0,L}, {vx,0,L}, {uy,0,ux}, {vy,0,vx}

it can give inconsistent results, even with ρ > 0 and L > 0. If you reorder to

{ux,0,L}, {uy,0,ux}, {vx,0,L}, {vy,0,vx}

then both approaches agree and return (1 - E^(-L^2 ρ)) L^2. The closest conclusion supported here is that the output changes because of a bug in the symbolic integrator’s handling of the integration order.

